  "fanTake": "Sunday at EverBank Stadium was the kind of afternoon that makes you question everything. The Patriots mustered exactly two field goals while Jacksonville's offense was a clinic in efficiency, converting every single red-zone trip into a touchdown—5 for 5, a perfect nightmare—while we managed 0 of 4. Our third-down defense was a revolving door (Jacksonville hit 8 of 12), our offense couldn't find traction (4 of 12), and Drake Maye's three turnovers became the punctuation on a performance he himself called unacceptable. At -0.25 EPA per play on offense and allowing 0.23 on defense, this wasn't close to competitive; it was a 29-point rout that left us staring at some hard truths about how we're building this team.",
